  "description": "Reads Caret-Separated Text (.cst), the plain-text format The Sims Online and Sims Steering Committee use for their text, where each value sits between two carets after its key: 1 ^Buy^. Follows the CST specification, reports malformed entries without losing the rest of a table, fills placeholders, and loads tables from a TSO install or from SSC's folders laid over one another.",
